<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle $110.50/dressed, active -trade.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle $110.50/dressed, active -trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nebraska feedlot cattle near midday Wednesday sold at $110.00 to $110.50 per cwt on a dressed basis, market sources said.</p>
<p>About 7,000 head sold in brisk trading, with further bids at $110.00 to $110.50 passed by some owners pricing cattle at $111.00 to $112.00, they said.</p>
<p>The dressed basis sales were steady to $0.50 lower, compared with Tuesday.</p>
<p>Sales also reportedly took place at $68.00 to $68.50 on a live basis, steady to $0.25 lower, compared with Tuesday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
